  "caveats": [
    "Only USDaf Jan-2025 is enumerated end-to-end (5 protocol + 15 branch + 1 governance = 21 contracts). May-2025 has only the 2 protocol-level contracts in scope; Jul-2025 only the CollateralRegistry. Full enumeration of May+Jul branches requires getTroveManager(i) reads on the CollateralRegistry.",
    "USDaf-v2 repo's deployment-manifest.json shows a 6-branch deployment (0xc6e32959 + 6 collateral branches ysyBOLD/scrvUSD/sUSDS/sfrxUSD/tBTC/WBTC18) that has ZERO BYTECODE on mainnet. That manifest is for testnet/staging, not production. The actual mainnet USDaf-v2 (per addresses/1.json) is the Jan-2025 3-branch WETH/wstETH/rETH deployment.",
    "safETH derivative-wrapper rotation: Swell/StaFi/Ankr have both 'old' and 'current' versions live on-chain. DL adapter still reads from the old versions for TVL accounting. The 13 OZ proxies cover both old and new; this brief only enumerates 7 README-named (current) ones.",
    "Asymmetry admin Safe 0x263b...ddeb threshold + signer membership not pulled in this brief \u2014 operator should run getOwners() + getThreshold() before relying on multisig-based governance for any scoping decision.",
    "Cantina competition contents are not parsed \u2014 the two Cantina URLs are referenced as 'discovery-ingest-placeholder' by v1 pipeline; the gold standard inherits the same gap. Operator should pull the Cantina reports.",
    "USDaf governance reads vote-weight from LQTY (Liquity's governance token) holders, which is unusual and worth confirming with the Asymmetry team before relying on it for an audit-scoping assumption.",
    "afCVX SimpleProxy is a custom non-standard proxy pattern (not OZ TUP, not ERC1967) \u2014 admin slot semantics differ; audit team should re-read the proxy contract carefully.",
    "Asymmetry main product deployer 0x318d0059efe546b5687fa6744af4339391153981 deployed afCVX + ASF + veASF \u2014 a single EOA that bridges these products. The deployer has no on-chain power post-deployment but operator should verify EOA hygiene."
  ]
}